+// Upstream derives the selection field by mixing the host terminal's OSC 11
+// background 28% toward white. On a single-hue phosphor palette that lands on
+// a desaturated grey (#050806 -> #4B4D4C), which is the one colour a
+// monochrome terminal cannot produce, and pairs it with an ANSI-white glyph
+// for a washed-out grey-on-grey block.
+//
+// A real VT220 had exactly two states: dark field with lit glyphs, and reverse
+// video. So emit SGR 7 and let the terminal swap its own default pair. The
+// field becomes the foreground rung and the glyphs the background rung, with
+// no colour named here at all -- so this follows the phosphor switch and the
+// light/dark toggle for free, on any profile.
+//
+// The colour-derivation helpers below are left in place (unused outside
+// #[cfg(test)]) so this patch stays a small, re-appliable diff across version
